# Files for the source distribution (sdist).
#
# The inherited manifest referenced the upstream CUDA layout:
#     include CMakeLists.txt
#     graft csrc
#     graft include
# `include/` does not exist in this fork -- it held upstream's CUDA headers -- so
# every sdist build printed "no directories found matching 'include'", and
# CMakeLists.txt is unused now that the wheel ships a prebuilt CPU DLL instead of
# compiling anything.
#
# csrc is kept deliberately: it is what build_manual.bat / build_linux.sh /
# build_termux.sh compile when someone wants to rebuild the kernel themselves,
# which is the difference between an sdist that is merely installable and one that
# is actually useful.
graft csrc
graft build_manual
graft docs_cpu
graft examples
# tools/ holds gen_api_reference.py and verify_help_examples.py, which regenerate and
# check docs_cpu/API_REFERENCE*.md from the tables in bitsandbytes_cpu_cli.py. The
# generated documents ARE shipped, so leaving the generators out would hand users the
# output of scripts they cannot run.
graft tools
# ...but not the Windows binaries inside it. `graft tools` takes the whole directory,
# and the four sector_*.exe disaster-recovery tools were 0.65 MB of a 1.36 MB sdist --
# nearly half its weight, on every platform, for binaries that cannot run on two of the
# three. Their .c sources stay in the sdist and in the repository.
global-exclude *.exe
global-exclude *.exe.manifest
include build_linux.sh
include build_termux.sh
include selftest_cpu.c
include README.md
include LICENSE
